```c
guest_regs->rax = -EPERM;
switch (guest_regs->rax) {
    case JAILHOUSE_HC_DISABLE:
        guest_regs->rax = shutdown(cpu_data);
```
Reason:
The fix involves modifying `guest_regs->rax` instead of `vmcb->rax`. By using `guest_regs->rax`, the intended values are preserved when the guest resumes, preventing the overwriting issue and ensuring that the hypercall handling operates correctly without losing critical information.

